            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0920" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./145</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 23.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1058</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to the Department’s telegram No.
                    24 of September 10, 1928, regarding the Pan American Airways, Incorporated, I
                    have the honor to report that representatives of this company, Messrs. Nagle and
                    MacGregor, were here recently for a few days in the interests of this company.
                    They were introduced by the Legation to President Vasquez and the Minister of
                    Finance to whom they outlined the company’s plans with respects to the
                    establishment of a commercial air service between Miami, Florida, and San Juan,
                    Porto Rico. The President and Minister de Moya stated that the establishment of
                    the proposed service would be cordially welcomed by the Dominican Government
                    which would gladly accord every possible facility and assistance.</p>
                <pb facs="0921" n="793" xml:id="pg793"/>
                <p>It is understood that Mr. Nagle will return to Santo Domingo in the near future
                    and will then endeavor to reach a formal agreement and undertaking with the
                    Government.</p>
                <p>The Legation was happy to accord to these gentlemen during their stay here every
                    possible and proper assistance.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Evan E. Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
